1
00:00:00,079 --> 00:00:03,529
Open the saved route in Edit and check its
Name and Description

2
00:00:03,529 --> 00:00:05,039
before changing its state.

3
00:00:05,449 --> 00:00:09,069
This is the fictional Community supply
loop from the route-planning lesson.

4
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:11,170
It has two prepared stops.

5
00:00:11,609 --> 00:00:15,800
Unit still says Assign at start time, and
Status is Draft.

6
00:00:16,250 --> 00:00:18,290
Practice in a separate training
department.

7
00:00:18,639 --> 00:00:23,639
Before using a real plan, verify its
locations, contacts and directions with

8
00:00:23,639 --> 00:00:25,430
the people responsible for the work.

9
00:00:25,520 --> 00:00:28,029
Change Status from Draft to Active.

10
00:00:28,430 --> 00:00:31,210
Scroll to the bottom and select Save
Changes.

11
00:00:31,599 --> 00:00:35,580
The returned Routes list shows Active
beside Community supply loop,

12
00:00:35,889 --> 00:00:38,040
and its Actions now include Start.

13
00:00:38,450 --> 00:00:42,390
The plan is ready for the start operation,
but this saved status alone

14
00:00:42,390 --> 00:00:44,329
does not show a unit executing it.

15
00:00:44,729 --> 00:00:48,720
The next step explicitly chooses the unit
and creates that execution.

16
00:00:48,930 --> 00:00:51,139
Select Start on the saved route row.

17
00:00:51,580 --> 00:00:55,590
The Start Route page asks for Assign Unit
and says to select the

18
00:00:55,590 --> 00:00:57,369
unit that will execute this route.

19
00:00:57,770 --> 00:01:00,340
Choose the fictional Community van from
the dropdown.

20
00:01:00,949 --> 00:01:03,760
Review the route name and this unit
selection together.

21
00:01:04,150 --> 00:01:07,709
In your department, choose the resource
responsible for these stops.

22
00:01:08,130 --> 00:01:11,730
The Start Route Now button is the action
that begins the execution;

23
00:01:12,140 --> 00:01:14,009
Cancel leaves this start form.

24
00:01:14,240 --> 00:01:16,339
Select Start Route Now once.

25
00:01:16,759 --> 00:01:21,470
The returned Route Instance page shows In
Progress in Instance Info, the

26
00:01:21,470 --> 00:01:23,990
unit identifier, and a Started time.

27
00:01:24,370 --> 00:01:27,769
Here the selected training van is
represented by unit number

28
00:01:27,849 --> 00:01:29,210
fifty-one thousand eight.

29
00:01:29,529 --> 00:01:33,000
Ended is a dash, and Progress is zero of
two.

30
00:01:33,440 --> 00:01:36,590
These saved instance details show that the
start succeeded.

31
00:01:37,010 --> 00:01:40,459
They do not say that either service stop
has already been completed.

32
00:01:40,599 --> 00:01:43,099
Scroll down to inspect Stop Timeline.

33
00:01:43,579 --> 00:01:47,000
Both entries are Pending in this newly
started instance, and the

34
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:48,929
progress remains zero of two.

35
00:01:49,490 --> 00:01:52,969
Use the status text and progress together
when reviewing a route.

36
00:01:53,330 --> 00:01:56,969
This recording has not checked into either
location, and the map does

37
00:01:56,969 --> 00:01:58,969
not display a generated road route.

38
00:01:59,299 --> 00:02:02,580
Starting an instance is an administration
step; verify

39
00:02:02,580 --> 00:02:06,600
navigation and actual field progress
separately before relying on them.

40
00:02:06,790 --> 00:02:10,670
Return to Routes and select In Progress in
the top action bar.

41
00:02:11,040 --> 00:02:15,280
The overview now contains the Community
supply loop card, its unit number,

42
00:02:15,449 --> 00:02:18,180
start time and zero-of-two stop count.

43
00:02:18,539 --> 00:02:20,629
Select View Details on that card.

44
00:02:21,039 --> 00:02:25,580
The same instance information returns with
In Progress and the original start time.

45
00:02:25,949 --> 00:02:29,340
This lets a supervisor find an executing
route again without

46
00:02:29,340 --> 00:02:30,840
starting another instance.

47
00:02:31,010 --> 00:02:34,979
Return to Routes and select History on the
Community supply loop row.

48
00:02:35,539 --> 00:02:39,390
Route History lists the stored execution
with Status, Unit,

49
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:42,140
Started, Ended and Stops columns.

50
00:02:42,550 --> 00:02:47,179
In this exercise there is one In Progress
row, a start time, no end

51
00:02:47,179 --> 00:02:50,029
time and zero of two completed stops.

52
00:02:50,460 --> 00:02:52,240
Detail opens that execution.

53
00:02:52,699 --> 00:02:56,349
Use this history when checking which
instance a progress report refers

54
00:02:56,349 --> 00:03:00,050
to, rather than treating the plan status
as the execution history.

55
00:03:00,160 --> 00:03:04,719
For this training check, return to Start
and select the same Community van while

56
00:03:04,719 --> 00:03:06,989
its first instance is still in progress.

57
00:03:07,379 --> 00:03:09,449
Select Start Route Now once.

58
00:03:09,910 --> 00:03:13,800
Resgrid returns Unit already has an active
route instance.

59
00:03:14,160 --> 00:03:17,149
This refusal means the second start did
not succeed.

60
00:03:17,530 --> 00:03:19,389
Do not keep retrying that unit.

61
00:03:19,770 --> 00:03:23,879
Review its existing route before deciding
whether another appropriate resource

62
00:03:23,879 --> 00:03:25,420
should take a different assignment.

63
00:03:25,519 --> 00:03:30,349
Leave the refused start with Cancel,
return to Routes and open History again.

64
00:03:30,789 --> 00:03:34,849
The recorded result still has the original
single In Progress instance

65
00:03:34,910 --> 00:03:36,940
with zero of two stops completed.

66
00:03:37,410 --> 00:03:41,860
Keep the distinction clear: prepare the
plan, start the intended unit,

67
00:03:42,140 --> 00:03:44,259
then inspect actual progress.

68
00:03:44,700 --> 00:03:48,110
This pattern can support search-and-rescue
logistics, security

69
00:03:48,110 --> 00:03:52,940
service visits, wildland supplies,
industrial response support, community

70
00:03:52,940 --> 00:03:57,140
paramedicine or mental health outreach, as
well as fire and E M S.

71
00:03:57,540 --> 00:04:00,869
Match the stops and assigned resource to
your department’s work.

